{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122788","id":4353566244,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA34mJA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122788","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122788.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122788.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122788","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122788/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122788/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122788/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/98cdbf6c254f0999f6a632164a8f9186833e1db5","number":122788,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add reusable result object to PhysicsDirectSpaceState3D.cast_motion","user":{"login":"leelokone","id":171243945,"node_id":"U_kgDOCjT5qQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171243945?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone","html_url":"https://github.com/leelokone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nPhysicsDirectSpaceState3D.cast_motion() currently returns a PackedFloat32Array, in C#, this creates a managed array for every call, causing avoidable allocations when the method is repeatedly used during physics processing.\r\n\r\nAlso callers that need additional information, such as the collision point and normal, collider RID and instance ID, shape index, or velocity at the contact point, must perform an additional get_rest_info() physics query, this requires another physics query and returns a result in dictionary causing more managed allocations, the native cast_motion() interface already supports an optional ShapeRestInfo, but this information is not exposed by the scripting API, Jolt implementation also does not currently support returning this information.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis PR changes the return type of `cast_motion()` to `bool`, indicating whether a collision did occur, and optional newly added reusable PhysicsCastMotionResult3D object can be passed to receive the safe and unsafe motion fractions, collision point and normal, collider RID and instance ID, collider shape index, and velocity at the collision point.\r\n\r\nThe result object is reset before each valid query and can be reused across calls, this avoids allocating a new managed result for every call, Jolt physics implementation has also been extended to return the collision that limits the motion.\r\n\r\n- Related proposal: godotengine/godot-proposals#15430\r\n\r\n### Benchmarks\r\n\r\nObserved result for a hit requiring full contact data\r\n\r\nJolt:\r\n- Legacy cast_motion() followed by get_rest_info(): 0.010727 ms/call, allocations 973 B/call\r\n- Reusable result: 0.004950 ms/call, 0 B/call\r\n- Time reduction: 53.9% (2.17x faster)\r\n\r\nGodotPhysics3D:\r\n- Legacy cast_motion() followed by get_rest_info(): 0.011327 ms/call, allocations  973 B/call\r\n- Reusable result: 0.005915 ms/call, 0 B/call\r\n- Time reduction: 47.8% (1.92x faster)\r\n\r\nThis is a compatibility-breaking API change, existing code that reads the returned array must migrate to the boolean return value and optionally pass a PhysicsCastMotionResult3D.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-25T00:48:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T08:14:19Z","closed_at":"2026-08-25T08:14:15Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f88c91563982d5ca3a8dcd556568737502887688","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"leelokone:physics-cast-motion-result","ref":"physics-cast-motion-result","repo":{"id":1345477712,"node_id":"R_kgDOUDJcUA","name":"godot","full_name":"leelokone/godot","owner":{"login":"leelokone","id":171243945,"node_id":"U_kgDOCjT5qQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171243945?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone","html_url":"https://github.com/leelokone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leelokone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Godot Engine – Multi-platform 2D and 3D game engine","homepage":"https://godotengine.org","